# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# Application (client) ID of the multi-tenant Azure app registration used for
# Outlook calendar import. This is a PUBLIC client id, not a secret — it is
# bundled into the built JS by design (MSAL PKCE public client).
#
# Leave it unset to disable the Outlook feature entirely; the app falls back to
# .ics import and manual entry.
#
# On Netlify this must be set as a build-time environment variable (Site
# settings -> Environment variables), since Vite inlines VITE_* at build time.
VITE_MS_CLIENT_ID=
